# Docs‑First Answers
- For architecture questions, summarize from: `/docs/10-architecture/*` and `/docs/maps/*`.
- For API questions, quote from `/docs/20-backend/openapi.json` and show example requests.
- For code‑level usage, cite `/docs/api/*` (TypeDoc). If symbol lacks TSDoc, propose it.
- If docs conflict with code, open a docs PR to reconcile before code changes.
- Before proposing new files, APIs, or docs, perform a codebase search for similar or related modules.
- Prefer modifying or extending existing modules/docs over creating new ones.
- If new artifacts are justified, update Modules.md, OpenAPI, and TypeDoc in the same PR and run `docs:all`.
